The dereference operator (<computeroutput>operator*</computeroutput>) provides access to the value or object pointed to by the iterator. Internally, it calls <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1intrusive__list__iterator_1a11f2bc99a1f478650b82546e2e5470d1" kindref="member">get_pointer()</ref></computeroutput> to obtain a pointer to the underlying value or object associated with the current node in the list, and then dereferences it to return a reference.</para>
<para>This allows the iterator to be used in a manner similar to standard C++ iterators, enabling direct access to the list element for reading or modification. </para>
